          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A long list of mathematical structures happens to have a classification that is in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+laced+Dynkin+diagrams"} simply laced Dynkin diagrams
            of types A, D and E (but excluding type B and C), for instance
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Platonic+solids"} Platonic solids
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+group"} special orthogonal group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SO
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(3)
                and of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+group"} special unitary group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SU
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
                (see at
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classification+of+finite+rotation+groups"} classification of finite rotation groups
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#Milnor57"} Milnor 57
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#Keenan03"} Keenan 03, theorem 4
            %li
